# Hash Map Collisions

A **collision** happens when two different keys hash to the same index in the underlying array. Since a hash map can only store one value per slot, it needs a strategy to handle this.

## Common Collision Resolution Techniques

**1. Chaining** — Each slot holds a list (or linked list) of entries. Colliding items are appended to that list.

**2. Open Addressing** — When a slot is taken, probe for the next available slot using a rule (linear probing, quadratic probing, double hashing, etc.).

